      "title": "Indian opposition figures lead march to police barricades around supreme court",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/12/india-election-protests-delhi-police-shut-metro-stations-ahead-march",
      "description": "<p>Thousands join rally to deliver petition calling for resignation of election commissioner</p><p>Delhi police have again obstructed protests in India’s capital as thousands of people returned to the streets, led by opposition leaders, to demand the resignation of the election commissioner.</p><p>After mass unrest in the capital over the weekend, when thousands were detained and harassed by police as they attempted to take part in a protest led by the gen Z Cockroach movement, on Monday the main opposition leaders led another procession through Delhi, this time to the supreme court.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/12/india-election-protests-delhi-police-shut-metro-stations-ahead-march\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-12T14:23:59"
    },
